  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory completed the safety chain: it screened neurologic/headache red flags, treated the headache in a vascular-risk context, maintained medication safety, tracked pending tests/results, and built executable follow-up with caregiver receipt. The doctor repeatedly avoided closing the case as simple neuralgia, escalated to urgent care when red flags would appear, and adjusted the plan as the family moved from refusal, to clinic evaluation, to pending results, to home monitoring and cardiology/intervention follow-up. At least two high-order points were actively completed with trajectory impact, especially discriminating neuralgia versus vascular emergency and dynamically reprioritizing when clinic/results barriers changed. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error or important non-chain blocker is evident, so the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
