      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO3 was triggered by recurrent posterior head pain in a high-risk vascular patient with a neuralgia diagnosis. The doctor repeatedly verified neurologic red flags, pain escalation, gait/mental status, vomiting and chest symptoms, then gave a tiered conclusion: current presentation could be observed when stable, but urgent evaluation was required if red flags emerged and follow-up remained necessary.",
